values ('a3c4d5e6-7f8a-4b83-8c23-3d4e5f6a7b83', 'statistics-for-the-behavioral-sciences', 'Statistics for the Behavioral Sciences', 'Frame statistics as disciplined reasoning about behavior, measurement, uncertainty, evidence, and ethical inference. Connect measurement and design, summarize distributions, build probability and estimation, test hypotheses with effect sizes and power, compare groups with t tests and ANOVA, handle categorical and nonparametric data, model correlation, regression, moderation, and mediation, introduce multilevel, factor, and missing-data methods, and synthesize through APA-style reporting and a capstone behavioral-science analysis.');

